# The materialized editor document is a checked-in, minified, single-line JSON
# artifact (~830 KB). Because it is one physical line, git's default content
# merge conflicts on ANY two changes to it -- including changes thousands of
# lines apart once its `html` payload is decoded. `merge=materialized-runtime`
# routes it to tools/git/merge_materialized_runtime.py, which merges the
# decoded payload and refuses anything it cannot compose safely.
#
# The driver is per-clone configuration, so enable it once with:
#     tools/git/install-merge-driver.sh
# Until you do, git falls back to its normal conflict behaviour for this path.
# Nothing breaks without it; you just keep conflicting.
native-ui/materialized/materialized-document.runtime.json merge=materialized-runtime
